title: "AEIB: Agent Evidence Interlock Boundary"
version: 0.4.1
date-released: 2026-10-08
url: "https://github.com/smaos-ai/smaos-ai-sandbox"
repository-code: "https://github.com/smaos-ai/smaos-ai-sandbox"
abstract: >
  AEIB (Agent Evidence Interlock Boundary) is an execution-integrity and deterministic 
  disposition boundary for autonomous agent systems. Under the stated model, it evaluates 
  pre-dispatch standing checks immediately before network dispatch, suppresses speculative 
  retries upon transport ambiguity, and provides single-flight target reconciliation probes 
  with Ed25519 cryptographic receipts and RFC 8785 JSON Canonicalization.
keywords:
  - "agentic AI"
  - "autonomous systems"
  - "DORA"
  - "EU AI Act"
  - "RFC 8785"
  - "idempotency"
